From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruno Castelló <bfcastello@gmail.com>
Date: TBD
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] hw/display/meson: compile ati_metal.m with Metal on Darwin

Conditionally adds ati_metal.m to the softmmu build when CONFIG_ATI_VGA
is enabled and the host is Darwin. Links the Metal framework only —
no Cocoa or QuartzCore, since the renderer writes directly into guest
VRAM via a zero-copy MTLBuffer and never opens a second window.

ati_metal.m and ati_vgpu3d.h live directly in hw/display/ as committed
project files, not embedded in patches.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Castelló <bfcastello@gmail.com>
---
 hw/display/meson.build | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/display/meson.build b/hw/display/meson.build
index ffecedbf70..d4e1c00000 100644
--- a/hw/display/meson.build
+++ b/hw/display/meson.build
@@ -62,6 +62,15 @@ system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_ARTIST', if_true: files('artist.c'))

 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_ATI_VGA', if_true: [files('ati.c', 'ati_2d.c', 'ati_dbg.c'), pixman])

+if host_machine.system() == 'darwin'
+  metal_fw = dependency('appleframeworks',
+                        modules: ['Metal'],
+                        required: false)
+  if metal_fw.found()
+    system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_ATI_VGA', if_true: [files('ati_metal.m'), metal_fw])
+  endif
+endif
+
 system_ss.add(when: [pvg, 'CONFIG_MAC_PVG_PCI'],     if_true: [files('apple-gfx.m', 'apple-gfx-pci.m')])
 system_ss.add(when: [pvg, 'CONFIG_MAC_PVG_MMIO'],    if_true: [files('apple-gfx.m', 'apple-gfx-mmio.m')])

